# ManaQuest Design System

Retro game-UI aesthetic. Dark base + neon accents + pixel-corner motifs. All defined in `themes/ManaQuest/static/css/theme.css` as CSS variables — never hardcode colors elsewhere, use the tokens.

## Color tokens (CSS vars)

| Var | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--bg` | `#0f1020` | Page background base |
| `--panel` | `#1a1c33` | Card / panel solid bg |
| `--panel-soft` | `#242848` | Panel gradient top |
| `--text` | `#eef0ff` | Primary text |
| `--muted` | `#b7b9d3` | Secondary text, meta, labels |
| `--accent` | `#9dff6a` | Primary accent (mana green) — top-left corners, h2 bars, CTA glow |
| `--accent-2` | `#7ad7ff` | Secondary accent (cyan) — bottom-right corners, links, hover glow |
| `--border` | `#3a3f67` | Borders, dividers, inset rings |

## Accent rules

- **Top-left** corner / **left** rail / **first** glyph → `--accent` (green)
- **Bottom-right** corner / **right** glow / **secondary** highlight → `--accent-2` (cyan)
- Links default `--accent-2`; hover `--accent`. Never invert.

## Typography

- **UI mono** (labels, slot chips, kickers, section headers, code-block lang): `"JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace`. Uppercase, `letter-spacing: 0.14em–0.16em`.
- **Body**: `Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif`. Line-height `1.65`.
- **Hero h1**: gradient text fill `--text → --accent-2 → --accent`, weight `800`.

## Motifs (must reuse, never reinvent)

- **`.panel`** — pixel corner brackets (green TL, cyan BR), scanline grid bg, inset glow + drop shadow.
- **`.section-header`** — `▣` glyph + mono uppercase title + dashed bottom divider + right-side `.section-slot` chip.
- **`.btn`** — gradient body + inner highlight + outer shadow. Hover lifts + cyan glow. `.btn-primary` adds green identity.

## Don'ts

- No hardcoded `#hex` outside `theme.css` — extend tokens instead.
- No new accent colors. If a third needed, add a token, document here.
- No solid white text — use `--text` (off-white).
- Never reverse corner color order (TL = green, BR = cyan, always).
